SUMMARY:2026 Canadian Engineering Graduate Studies Fair
DESCRIPTION:Are you considering graduate studies and want to learn more about engineering graduate programs across Canada? The University of Toronto is part of the Canadian Graduate Engineering Consortium (CGEC)\, where we collaborate with Canadian universities to provide prospective students with information about our graduate engineering programs. \nJoin us for our graduate studies fair on September 16\, from 1:00 p.m. – 4:00 p.m. in the Bahen Centre lobby. \nDuring this event\, you’ll have the chance to talk to faculty\, current graduate students and admissions experts who can answer your questions about graduate programs in engineering. Drop by and discover how an engineering graduate degree can accelerate your career and academic goals! \nThe following U of T Engineering graduate departments will be available to share info about their programs and answer your questions: \n\nDepartment of Chemical Engineering & Applied Chemistry (ChemE)\nDepartment of Civil & Mineral Engineering (CivMin)\nDepartment of Materials Science & Engineering (MSE)\nDepartment of Mechanical & Industrial Engineering (MIE)\nThe Edward S. Rogers Sr. Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE)\nUniversity of Toronto Institute for Aerospace Studies (UTIAS)\nInstitute of Biomedical Engineering (BME)\n\nRepresentatives from the following universities will be also be available: \n\nMcMaster University\nQueen’s University\nToronto Metropolitan University\nUniversity of British Columbia\nUniversity of Waterloo\nWestern University\nYork University\n\nRegister here today.
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/canadian-engineering-graduate-studies-fair-2026/
LOCATION:Bahen Centre for Information Technology\, Atrium area\, 40 St George St
CATEGORIES:Info sessions
END:VEVENT
